# No orphaned words

Do not leave a single word alone on the last line of a paragraph, heading, blurb, or label.

This covers page copy, product and pattern text, wrapping button labels, and any other customer-facing block.

## How the site prevents it

`body` in `src/app/globals.css` sets `text-wrap: pretty`, which asks the browser to avoid a one-word last line. Leave that in place.

Short headings that should even out can use the `text-balance` utility (`text-wrap: balance`).

## When pretty is not enough

`text-wrap: pretty` is a hint. A narrow column, a bold phrase, or an inline icon can still strand one word. The about page stranded "local" this way.

When that happens, join the last two words with a non-breaking space so they wrap together:

- In JSX text: `are&nbsp;local`
- In a JS string: `"are\u00A0local"`

Check the block at phone, tablet, and desktop widths. One width looking fine is not enough.

## Examples

- Bad: the last line is only "local."
- Good: "are local." stays on one line together.
